  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "The present progressive in Spanish is formed with a conjugated form of *estar* plus a gerund (/-ndo/ form) of the main verb: *Estoy pensando* ('I am thinking'), *Estamos viviendo* ('We are living'), *Están escribiendo* ('They are writing'). \nThe gerund is invariable and does not change for number or gender. Use the progressive to describe actions in progress at the moment of speaking; unlike English, it is not normally used for future plans."
    }
